      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=140",
      "html": "<p>Scientific name: Pseudexostoma brachysoma Chu, 1979. Family: Sisoridae. Size: 153 mm (6\") SL. IUCN Red List: Not Evaluated.</p><p>Type locality: hill stream running into the Nu River, near Laowo, Yunlong Xian [now Lushi County, Nujiang Prefecture], Yunnan Province, China.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=140",
      "html": "<p>Asia: known only from the middle and lower Nujiang (=Salween) basin, China.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "reproduction",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=140",
      "html": "<p>Breeding: unreported. There is no breeding report.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "notes",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=140",
      "html": "<p>Identification: continuous post-labial groove, gill openings not extending onto the venter, heterodont dentition (different types of teeth) in both jaws. The outer teeth are shovel-shaped and sparsely arranged in one or two rows whilst the inner teeth are conical and numerous. The tooth patches are separated in the upper jaw. 16–18 branched pectoral rays.</p>"
    },
    {
